ltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"among the optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex. The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent edge. Tours read the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simple graph, as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"text":" documents; nil below three vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tour is determined for integer weights. With floating-point weights it is optimal for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sums as computed, and chosen by the same rule on them, so which of several equal tours"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes out, and its orientation, can depend on rounding."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The table, 2ⁿ⁻¹ · (n − 1) weights and as many validity bytes, fits in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"4 GiB: at most 25 vertices with 8-byte weights, 26 with 4-byte ones; no weight is NaN or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"infinite; the sum along any path fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"W","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Θ(2ⁿ n²) time and Θ(2ⁿ n) memory: n = 20 takes 80 MB of table for 8-byte"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weights on a complete graph, and 90 MB on another (the validity flags)."}]}],"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc